n Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's open governor's race pits Democrat Xavier Becerra against Republican Steve Hilton, with Gavin Newsom term-limited and off the ballot. The state's D+12 lean favors Democrats, and every major rating outlet calls the race Solid or Safe Democratic. Polling from September and October consistently shows Becerra ahead by double digits, with recent surveys ranging from 16 to 27 points, including polls sponsored by Republican-leaning firms. Prediction markets price Becerra's chances around 96 to 97 percent.\n\nHilton has slightly out-raised Becerra and holds more cash on hand, and coverage notes voter dissatisfaction with the state's direction, yet his campaigning has shown little measurable dent in the numbers. The main open questions are the final margin and turnout, not the likely winner. Becerra enters the closing stretch as a strong favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 14.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9677, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9665, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9687, "margin